{"name":"Woodland Soul","hex":"#127a49","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"woodland","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a creature or object: growing, living, or existing in a woodland.","Having the character of a woodland."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Land covered with woody vegetation.","A low-density forest."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woodland"},{"term":"soul","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The spirit or essence of a person usually thought to consist of one's thoughts and personality, often believed to live on after the person's death.","The spirit or essence of anything."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characteristic of or pertaining to African American culture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soul"}],"entries":[{"title":"Woodland","blocks":[{"text":"A woodland is, in the broad sense, land covered with woody plants, or in a narrow sense, synonymous with wood, a low-density forest forming open habitats with plenty of sunlight and limited shade. Some savannas may also be woodlands, such as savanna woodland, where trees and shrubs form a light canopy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Woodland%2C_Bogside_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2215308.jpg/330px-Woodland%2C_Bogside_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2215308.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodland"},{"title":"Soul","blocks":[{"text":"In religion and philosophy, the soul is the immaterial aspect or essence of a living being. It is typically believed to be immortal and to exist apart from the material world. Anthropologists and psychologists have found that most humans believe in the existence of a soul or spirit, and that they have cross-culturally distinguished between the soul and the material body."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Schiavonetti_Soul_leaving_body_1808.jpg/330px-